%I A398919 #35 Sep 17 2026 23:58:57
%S A398919 0,1,3,25,120,2115,17955,637625,19954200,2108673405
%N A398919 Number of nonempty sets of pairwise commuting derangements of [n].
%F A398919 Let B_k(n) be the number of k-element sets of pairwise commuting derangements of [n]. Then a(n) = Sum_{k>=1} B_k(n).
%F A398919 B_k(n) = (n!/k!) * Sum_{r=1..k} Stirling1(k,r)*[x^n]G_r(x),
%F A398919 G_r(x) = exp(Sum_{m>=1} q_r(m)*x^m/m),
%F A398919 q_r(m) = Sum_{j=0..r} (-1)^j*binomial(r,j)*A160870(m,r-j).
%F A398919 Here q_r(m) is the number of subgroups H of index m in Z^r such that none of the standard generators e_1,...,e_r belongs to H; equivalently, each e_i acts without fixed points on the corresponding transitive Z^r-orbit.
%e A398919 For n=3, the only derangements are (123) and (132), and they commute. Thus the nonempty sets of pairwise commuting derangements are {(123)}, {(132)}, and {(123),(132)}, giving a(3)=3.
%Y A398919 Cf. A000166 (derangements), A160870 (subgroups of finite index in free Abelian groups), A399972 (nonempty sets of pairwise commuting permutations).
%K A398919 nonn,more,new
%O A398919 1,3
%A A398919 _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 17 2026
